+# ext acceptance gate (spec §6) and contract-test skeleton
+
+This directory makes the L2 spec's six acceptance gates executable. It owns the
+judgment rules, the input contracts, the failure definitions and the artifact
+format. It does **not** own the measurement: real G1/G2 browser sampling belongs
+to hapi-dsh's warm Host/Chromium, and G3/G5/G6 sampling belongs to the store /
+installation / upgrade harnesses. A sampler that did not run is `FAIL`
+(`NOT_EXECUTED`), never a skipped gate.
+
+## Layout
+
+```text
+ext/
+  scripts/
+    accept-ext.mjs                 # unified serial entry point
+    lib/                           # args, config, exec, samples, verdict, normalize, artifact
+    gates/                         # G1..G6 verdict functions + spec thresholds
+    adapters/hapi-dsh.mjs          # partial adapters for existing hapi-dsh commands
+    fixtures/
+      schema/g1..g6.schema.json    # input contracts for real samplers
+      build.mjs                    # deterministic pass/fail fixtures for --self-check
+  tests/
+    contracts/                     # 0001 (6) / 0002 (4) / 0003 (5) contract names
+    profile/                       # eight feature-switch combinations
+    distribution/                  # install idempotency, override conflicts, rollback
+  releases/
+    active-rc.json
+    manifest.schema.json
+    compatibility-matrix.template.md|json
+    <rc>/acceptance-<time>.json    # raw JSON + per-frame samples + summary
+```
+
+## Commands
+
+```sh
+# help
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --help
+
+# prove the verdict functions (not the product)
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --gate G4 --self-check
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --all --self-check
+
+# print the executable measurement plan and sampler interface
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --all --plan
+
+# judge one recorded dataset (no sampler)
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --gate G1 --fixture <dataset.json>
+
+# live run: spawn the configured sampler, single attempt per gate, serial
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --gate G1
+node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs --all --timeout-ms 1200000
+
+# skeleton contract tests (all behavioural tests are it.skip until their patch lands)
+node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config ext/vitest.config.ts
+```
+
+Exit codes: `0` every selected gate `PASS` / `SELF-CHECK-PASS` / plan printed,
+`1` any `FAIL`, `2` usage error. Artifacts are written to
+`ext/releases/<rc>/acceptance-<time>.json`.
+
+## Verdict rules that never relax
+
+- One measurement attempt per sample. A non-1 `attempt`, a process retry record or
+  a reused sample id is `SAMPLE_RETRY_OVERWRITE` and fails the gate.
+- Required sample counts are per spec (20 / 20 / 100 commits / 324 cases /
+  3 install runs / 3 rounds). Fewer samples is `MISSING_SAMPLES`.
+- A timeout, nonzero sampler exit, unreadable payload or unconfigured sampler is
+  `FAIL`; there is no default `PASS`.
+- G1 non-cold samples (display cache not cleared) do not count toward the 20.
+- G2 requires exactly ten dual-pane samples and per-frame anchor values; a
+  reported maximum that disagrees with the frame series is a failure.
+- G3 enforces B=2000, events ≤5000, body ≤12 MiB, peak ≤2B, traversal ≥20,000
+  and DOM ≤15,000 / body markers ≤100.
+- G4 normalizes ids/timestamps/revisions, preserves event order, and requires
+  zero difference against original rc.3 for all eight switch combinations; no
+  provider ⇒ 0 registrations and 0 new windows.
+- G5 requires all eight handshake fields tampered with, each diagnosed with zero
+  business forwards; repeat installs must report an empty diff.
+- G6 health-check rollback must complete within 30 s; old release active on every
+  injection; no duplicated queue/approval action.
+
+## Live samplers
+
+Each gate accepts a command through `HAPI_DSH_EXT_<G>_CMD` (a JSON dataset on
+stdout, or a JSON file path printed as the last line). Where an existing
+hapi-dsh command emits usable evidence, it is wired as a **partial** default and
+the judge fails on what it cannot prove:
+
+| gate | live sampler env | existing default | current evidence level |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| G1 | `HAPI_DSH_EXT_G1_CMD` | hapi-dsh `e2e/ui-cli.ts` (warm synthetic acceptance) | partial: warm opens only, no 20 cold opens, no per-open history proof |
+| G2 | `HAPI_DSH_EXT_G2_CMD` | hapi-dsh `e2e/ui-cli.ts` | partial: wheel/anchor frames only, no 20 paging samples, no editor/draft proof per sample |
+| G3 | `HAPI_DSH_EXT_G3_CMD` | none | judgment only; store/assembler instrumentation not implemented |
+| G4 | `HAPI_DSH_EXT_G4_CMD` | none | judgment + normalizer + fixture matrix; real synthetic profile matrix runner not implemented |
+| G5 | `HAPI_DSH_EXT_G5_CMD` | hapi-dsh `scripts/distribution-smoke.mjs` (legacy tarball smoke) | partial: clean install only, no ext bundle, no Runner identity, no tamper matrix |
+| G6 | `HAPI_DSH_EXT_G6_CMD` | none | judgment only; upgrade/rollback harness not implemented |
+
+The real G1 sampler must be a 20× cold-open production probe with per-run
+display-cache clearing (hapi-dsh `scripts/probe-cold-open.mjs` is the closest
+existing probe but is diagnostic, not a 20-sample gate sampler). G3/G4/G6
+samplers should be added beside the harness they measure, not inside this
+directory.
+
+`HAPI_DSH_ROOT` (default `/mnt/cache/src/hapi-dsh`) and `HAPI_DSH_TEST_ROOT`
+(default `/mnt/cache/data-cache`) select the Host/Chromium tools and their
+temporary artifacts. This repository does not modify hapi-dsh.
+
+## What a `SELF-CHECK-PASS` means
+
+It means: the gate judge accepts a spec-conforming synthetic dataset, rejects
+every single-rule fail fixture, rejects missing/duplicated/retried samples,
+rejects a gate mismatch, and turns runner failures (not executed, timeout,
+nonzero exit, bad payload, missing dataset) into `FAIL`. It says nothing about
+the product and must not be cited as a passed gate.
+
+Per-frame samples produced by the judge (G1 observation frames, G2 anchor
+frames) are embedded in the acceptance artifact under `frameSamples`.
