+# ADR 0001: history source provider
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted for the `ext/0.2.1-rc.3` branch. Touches `packages/api/session-controller`,
+`packages/client/ui-conversation`, and `packages/client/ui-chat` only. Applied
+after `0002-mounted-chat.patch` in the series because both patches extend
+`ChatView`/`contract/slots.ts`.
+
+## Context
+
+The official client has exactly one history source per Session generation:
+`SessionEventStream`, opened off the addressed journal and published as one
+contiguous `MutableSessionEventSource` window. A downstream extension that owns
+a different source of history (an external store, a per-message index, a
+non-journal transport) has only bad options: reimplement the Session object,
+replace the window behind the official assembler, or keep a second controller
+beside the official one. All of them break either the Session execution
+identity or the Conversation identity rules.
+
+The traffic this patch has to carry:
+
+- one provider connection for a Session generation, chosen before the
+  generation opens, so history is never opened twice;
+- one independent, releasable reading window per Pane, so two distant Panes
+  cannot both be clamped to one bounded contiguous window;
+- snapshot/delta joining by source version, so the tail committed between a
+  snapshot and a subscription is not lost;
+- window replacement through the official assembler, so derived nodes belong to
+  the standard lifecycle and release with the window.
+
+## Decision
+
+Patch 0001 adds a versioned history-source contract inside
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller/client`:
+
+```ts
+interface HistorySnapshotV1 {
+  version: SourceVersion
+  entries: readonly SessionEventLikeEntry[]
+  before: Cursor | null
+  after: Cursor | null
+  hasBefore: boolean
+  hasAfter: boolean
+}
+type HistoryReadV1 =
+  | { kind: 'latest' }
+  | { kind: 'before' | 'after'; cursor: Cursor }
+  | { kind: 'around'; target: HistoryTarget }
+interface HistoryDeltaV1 {
+  base: SourceVersion
+  version: SourceVersion
+  changes: readonly SessionEventChange[]
+  headChanged: boolean
+}
+interface HistoryFeedV1 {
+  initial: HistorySnapshotV1
+  read(request: HistoryReadV1, budget: Budget, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<HistorySnapshotV1>
+  changes(after: SourceVersion, signal: AbortSignal): AsyncIterable<HistoryDeltaV1>
+  release(): void
+}
+interface HistorySourceV1 {
+  openWindow(viewId: string, budget: Budget, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<HistoryFeedV1>
+  release(): void
+}
+interface HistoryProviderV1 {
+  id: string
+  matches(sessionId: SessionId): boolean
+  open(sessionId: SessionId, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<HistorySourceV1>
+}
+interface HistorySourcesV1 {
+  version: 1
+  register(provider: HistoryProviderV1): Stop
+}
+declare function historyExtension(sessions: ISessions): HistorySourcesV1 | undefined
+```
+
+Ownership and state boundaries:
+
+- `ISessions.historySource` is an optional public property; `historyExtension()`
+  is its thin accessor and probes no private field. With the built-in switch
+  `DSH_CLIENT_HISTORY_SOURCE=off`, the property is absent and the accessor
+  returns undefined.
+- Providers are selected in `ClientSessions.retain`, before the generation's
+  first `open()`. Zero matches keep `SessionEventStream` untouched; two matches
+  throw `HistorySourceError` code `PROVIDER_CONFLICT` before any history read or
+  provider window opening. Unregistering a provider refuses new bindings and
+  leaves existing connections alone.
+- Each Session generation owns one `HistorySourceV1`. `SessionHistoryConnection`
+  opens one feed per view id and reuses the live feed for the same id, so a
+  re-rendered Pane does not open another window. Releasing a feed never releases
+  execution; the connection closes on Session disposal or resync.
+- The default Session window is the first connection window (`viewId: 'session'`).
+  Its opening snapshot is applied, then deltas are followed from
+  `initial.version`. A delta whose `base` is not the held version is not appended
+  across the gap: the window re-reads `{ kind: 'latest' }` and replaces itself.
+- `ISession.historyRead` is an optional per-generation handle exposing
+  `openView(viewId, budget?, signal?)`. It is absent with no provider or before
+  the generation opens.
+
+Conversation side (`ui-conversation`):
+
+- `ConversationBinding.historyView(viewId)` acquires a refcounted reading scope;
+  the same view id returns the same live window with another lease. The scope is
+  created and released by the official binding lifecycle: `release()` on the
+  last lease releases the provider feed, and binding disposal releases every
+  remaining scope.
+- A scope owns one private `ConversationNodeAssembler`. Window replacement calls
+  the official `replaceWindow` (clear and rebuild); no node withdrawal method is
+  exposed. Page loads prepend/append through the same assembler.
+- One page read is in flight per window; a newer navigation request replaces the
+  single pending one and all its waiters settle on the resulting window.
+  Identical pending requests merge.
+- Changes applied but not yet published are bounded at **256 changes or 1MiB**.
+  Exceeding the bound does not drop changes: it triggers a newest-window resync
+  and replacement. Publication is frame-paced when `requestAnimationFrame`
+  exists, so a synchronous provider burst cannot grow the buffer past the bound.
+- A window detached from the head (`hasAfter`) never appends live tail changes
+  across the gap; it only raises `headChanged`.
+
+Chat side (`ui-chat`):
+
+- `ChatViewInjected.hooks.historyPaging` publishes the attached window's
+  `{ busy, hasOlder, detached, headChanged }`. The optional Cordis service
+  `historyPagingConsumer` supplies the per-Session source; without it a stable
+  empty source keeps the official `hasMore`/`loadingOlder` behavior.
+- `ChatView` reads that hook for the older-history affordance only. Session
+  submission, queue, approvals, and the official scroll controller still resolve
+  the Session, not a window.
+
+Capability detection is a frozen read-only declaration: `capabilities.historySource === 1`.
+
+## Default-path invariance
+
+With no provider registered (or with the capability switched off):
+
+- `historyExtension()` is undefined or a registry with zero providers;
+- no `historyRead` handle is exposed, `SessionEventStream` is the only history
+  source, and the `follow`/`page` call sequence is unchanged;
+- `ConversationBinding.historyView` returns undefined and no window feed is
+  opened;
+- the Chat view reads the stable empty paging source, so its injected values and
+  rendered affordance are the official ones.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A provider cannot change execution identity, queueing, approvals, reconnection,
+  or persistence: the patch never touches those paths.
+- Windows share the Session write side but not read state, so one Pane paging
+  older history cannot extend another Pane's window.
+- Provider failure during opening fails the generation open (the retain
+  `ready` promise rejects) and sets `openState: 'error'`; `openError` stays the
+  Remote-failure channel, so a failed provider open carries its structured
+  `HistorySourceError` code on the rejection instead.
+- The scope assembles every registered Conversation target for its window. A
+  future patch can restrict activation to the targets a Pane renders.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `packages/api/session-controller/tests/history-source.client.spec.ts`:
+  `default-provider-unchanged`, `provider-conflict`, `snapshot-tail-no-gap`.
+- `packages/client/ui-conversation/tests/history-source.client.spec.ts`:
+  `two-views-independent`, `replace-releases-nodes`, `release-keeps-execution`.
+- `pnpm --filter` bundles for the three touched packages succeed after the host
+  type face is built; the client type face still reports the checkout's
+  pre-existing missing generated `*/remote` declarations only.
+- Touched-package suites: 146 of 147 test files green; the single failure is the
+  unbuilt native `system.node` binding in `projection-discovery.host.spec.ts`,
+  unrelated to this patch.
+
+## Deferred
+
+- Per-Pane paging operations in `ChatView` (the official `loadOlder` still drives
+  the default window; a Pane that owns a scope calls `scope.read` itself).
+- Provider handshake identity in the release manifest (distribution concern).
+- `historyPagingConsumer` currently publishes one window per Session; a
+  multi-Pane host supplies distinct view ids through `ConversationBinding.historyView`.
