+# ADR 0002: mounted Chat control
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted for the `ext/0.2.1-rc.3` branch. Applies to `packages/client/ui-chat` only.
+
+## Context
+
+Downstream extensions need to drive and observe one attached Chat view: read the
+reader position, load older history, land on a durable target, and return to the
+live tail. Today that is only possible through private DOM probing, synthetic
+gestures, or a second scroll controller beside the official one — both forbid
+the committed behavior of the official path and race its anchoring.
+
+The extension must not fork the Chat view: the official view keeps sole ownership
+of the scrollport, reading policy, and history paging. What is missing is a
+public, read-only-to-write-restricted control face that an attached view hands
+to an interested consumer, with promises that mean "the committed window and its
+layout are in place", not "a request was sent".
+
+## Decision
+
+Patch 0002 adds a versioned mounted-control contract inside
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-chat/client`:
+
+```ts
+interface ReadingSnapshotV1 {
+  revision: number
+  anchor: { key: string; top: number } | null
+  following: boolean
+  hasOlder: boolean
+  busy: boolean
+}
+
+interface MountedChatV1 {
+  readonly version: 1
+  read(): ReadingSnapshotV1
+  subscribe(listener: () => void): Stop
+  loadOlder(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<void>
+  reveal(target: HistoryTarget, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<void>
+  toLatest(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<void>
+}
+
+interface MountedChatInjectionV1 {
+  onMountedChat?: (control: MountedChatV1 | null) => void
+}
+```
+
+Ownership and delivery rules:
+
+- `ChatView` creates exactly one control per mounted view and delivers it once;
+  re-renders keep the same handle. Unmount delivers `null`.
+- After unmount every call rejects: async methods reject with `MountedChatError`
+  code `DISPOSED`, sync calls throw the same error. Cancellation rejects with an
+  `AbortError`. An unreachable reveal rejects with `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE`.
+- `loadOlder` and `reveal` resolve from a committed render, after the prepended
+  window and its layout anchoring are applied. `reveal` pages history through
+  the official jump loader when the target is outside the window.
+- `toLatest` first asks the source for the newest window. A windowed history
+  source supplies `MountedChatSourceV1.readLatest` so an older retained window
+  is replaced by the source head before landing; the default live window always
+  follows the head and needs no read. A failed head read rejects and leaves the
+  current window untouched.
+- Reading facts publish only from committed layout, with a monotonic `revision`.
+
+Capability detection is a frozen read-only declaration exported with the
+contract: `capabilities.mountedChat === 1`. Consumers probe that value instead
+of private fields or version strings. A build-time switch
+`DSH_CLIENT_MOUNTED_CHAT=off` removes the declaration and stops delivery.
+
+Consumer wiring: a feature plugin provides the optional Cordis service
+`mountedChatConsumer: MountedChatConsumerV1`; the Chat plugin reads it when
+building `conversation.view` injected values and installs `onMountedChat` (and,
+when supplied, `readLatest`) on `ChatViewInjected`.
+
+## Default-path invariance
+
+With no consumer service, or with the capability switched off:
+
+- no control object is created, no reading facts are published, no listener is
+  registered;
+- the view's injected values differ only by absent optional fields;
+- no additional Session call, history read, or scroll write happens.
+
+This is the binding acceptance condition: the default path is byte-for-byte the
+official behavior; only register-and-consume activates the extension.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The mount/unmount lifecycle, not a global owner, defines the handle's identity,
+  so two visible Chat views hand out two independent handles.
+- The control cannot reconfigure scroll policy, cancel native execution, or
+  mutate Session state beyond official history paging.
+- `reveal` needs the target's stable node key and durable sequence; a caller that
+  only has a display ordinal cannot construct one.
+- The optional `readLatest` seam is consumed through the same consumer service so
+  patch 0002 remains self-contained; a windowed history source (patch 0001)
+  supplies it when present.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `packages/client/ui-chat/tests/mounted-chat.client.spec.tsx`:
+  `capability-declaration`, `mounted-owner-singleton`,
+  `older-resolves-after-layout`, `latest-fetches-head`,
+  `latest failure preserves the current window`, `unmount-invalidates-handle`.
+- Full `packages/client/ui-chat` suite (52 files, 850 tests) stays green.
+- `pnpm --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-chat bundle` succeeds after the
+  package type faces are built (`tsc -b tsconfig.host.json` and
+  `tsconfig.client.json`); `lib/client.js` contains the mounted-control contract.
+
+## Deferred
+
+- No handshake identity field yet: distribution-level capability reporting
+  belongs to the release manifest, not this package.
+- Only the four named contract tests plus two supporting behaviors are pinned;
+  concurrent-operation serialization, multi-pane reveal arbitration, and
+  measure-before-publish belong to the window-commit patch.
