+# ADR 0007: Mounted history uses the official reading owner
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted for the local HAPI DSH extension; upstream proposal drafted.
+
+## Decision
+
+The mounted Chat control's `loadOlder` delegates to the same `ChatNavigation.loadEarlier` used by the paging button. Both establish the official paging anchor and release tail following before reading. The injected loader and navigation retain the Session loader's Promise. A following-state render is not a page result; the operation waits for the read to settle and the official layout opportunity before resolving. This also settles cached folded pages whose outer node order did not change. Older void-returning view loaders keep the existing committed-render checks.
+
+The optional `preparePageCommit()` method lets an external history owner ask this mounted reader to sample its current position immediately before publishing source rows. The official viewport retains that semantic position and restores it during its layout pass. Feature plugins do not measure or write scroll offsets to compensate this publication. The method is delivered only with the existing mounted-Chat extension; disabling that extension preserves the default path.
+
+Mounted-control delivery includes the owning Chat root element, including on unmount. A shared Client graph can associate each portal occurrence with its Pane without using Session identity or creating a graph per Pane. Offscreen preparation occurrences remain distinct from visible readers.
+
+Native scroll samples attributed to the reader release an outstanding paging anchor before resize compensation. A page can begin during an existing touch drag or wheel momentum, so waiting for another touchstart or wheel event would undo that movement. The publication boundary samples the reader again and preserves the new position.
+
+## Verification
+
+Mounted-Chat component tests check that programmatic paging releases follow and remains pending while an older layout is still loading. HAPI DSH's source-reader test delays the official completion after the source cursor advances, then walks folded pages until earlier readable content appears. The release browser journey must reach three earlier readable positions and return over the resident history without duplicate reads or anchor jumps.
+
+Externally paged histories can supply `chatPresentationConsumer.presentation(sessionId)` to keep process summaries in the reading flow. Its optional `virtualizeGroupMembers` choice uses the Chat Node order directly, with each complete Node in one stable virtual row. It does not read the independent process-group projection or split a Node into group-dependent rendering parts. Without this consumer, grouping and whole-Turn folding keep their existing preferences. A component regression admits three older slices before process grouping publishes and retains the existing row DOM; the old grouped route fails this assertion.
+
+Virtual layout correction uses the browser-clamped scroll offset without querying full scroll metrics. It does not publish follow metrics, so it needs no `scrollHeight` query; browser sampling identified that query in virtual commits as the dominant forced-layout cost. Source integrations use the same reader sampling before older, newer and live window publications.
