@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# ext releases
+
+Artifacts for one ext build live under `ext/releases/<rc>/`. `<rc>` defaults to
+the `active` value in `active-rc.json` and can be overridden with `--rc`.
+
+## Files
+
+- `active-rc.json` — the single active rc. Old tags, packages and patch series
+  are never overwritten; a new build gets a new release directory.
+- `manifest.schema.json` — release manifest schema. Required fields:
+  `upstreamVersion`, `upstreamCommit`, `patchSetSha256`, `packageSetSha256`,
+  `capabilities` (`historySource` / `mountedChat` / `windowCommit`),
+  `compositionVersion`, `protocol`, plus `extRelease`. The manifest records the
+  real upstream version and full commit, never just the ext version.
+- `compatibility-matrix.template.md` / `.json` — append-only compatibility rows.
+  A `PASS` row requires G1–G6 artifacts for the exact build tuple.
+- `acceptance-<time>.json` — one `accept-ext` run (`accept-ext/1`): raw sampler
+  JSON, per-frame samples and the per-gate summary. Written by
+  `node ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs`. Existing artifacts are never edited.
+- `plan-<time>.json` — the executable measurement plan and sampler interface
+  printed by `--plan`.
+- `*-stdout.log` / `*-stderr.log` — raw sampler output for a live run.
+
+## Acceptance artifact rules
+
+- One attempt per gate. Failed samples stay in the artifact; the runner has no
+  retry path that could overwrite them.
+- A gate with missing samples, a timeout, a nonzero sampler exit, an unreadable
+  payload or `NOT_EXECUTED` is `FAIL`. There is no default `PASS`.
+- `mode: "self-check"` with `SELF-CHECK-PASS` proves the verdict functions accept
+  a spec-conforming fixture and reject each fail fixture plus the runner failure
+  rules. It is not product acceptance and must never be reported as a passed
+  gate.
+- `mode: "live"` is the only mode that can produce a gate `PASS`. The sampler
+  command is configured per gate with `HAPI_DSH_EXT_<G>_CMD` (see the top-level
+  `ext/README.md`).
+
+## Release manifest
+
+`manifest.schema.json` is the contract for `manifest.json` inside the bundled
+tgz. `packageSetSha256` covers the built package tarball set;
+`patchSetSha256` covers the ordered patch series. Both 64-hex and the full
+upstream commit are mandatory so a release cannot be re-pointed to a different
+upstream without a new manifest.
