@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# ext compatibility matrix (template)
+
+Append-only. One row per accepted ext release. A row is evidence, not a plan:
+`PASS` may only be written after the G1–G6 artifacts for that exact build exist
+under `ext/releases/<rc>/`, and every gate cites its artifact path. `NOT-RUN`,
+skipped and timed-out gates are never compatible, even when older rows pass.
+
+Compatibility is only claimed for the exact tuple below. Any change to
+`upstreamCommit`, `patchSetSha256`, `packageSetSha256`, `capabilities`,
+`compositionVersion` or `protocol` creates a new row.
+
+| upstreamVersion | upstreamCommit | extRelease | patchSetSha256 | packageSetSha256 | capabilities (h/m/w) | compositionVersion | protocol | Host | 2× Runner | clean install | repeat install (×2, no diff) | upgrade e1→e2 | rollback e2→e1 | G1–G6 artifacts | status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0.2.1-rc.3 | 1f81c047fc48fa190a683e469daa699857e9afe8 | 0.2.1-rc.3.ext.1 | `<64-hex>` | `<64-hex>` | 1/1/1 | `<compositionVersion>` | 2 | `<PASS/FAIL/NOT-RUN>` | `<...>` | `<...>` | `<...>` | `<...>` | `<...>` | `ext/releases/0.2.1-rc.3/acceptance-<time>.json` | draft |
+
+## Rules
+
+- Mixed-version window: while any node is still on the old release, the identity
+  match fails and business channels stay closed. A matrix row cannot claim
+  compatibility for a mixed host/runner pair.
+- The health-check window is 30 s. A rollback slower than that is a failed row
+  even when the old release ends up active.
+- At least two previous releases stay installed and intact.
+- Rollback restores the release pointer, profile manifest/lock and client assets.
+  It never rewrites session logs, queues, approvals or native logs.
+- Cross-upstream-rc rollback is only claimable after a data-compatibility
+  rehearsal passes; the ext release itself performs no persistence-format
+  migration.
+- Never overwrite an old row, old tag, old package or old patch series. Supersede
+  with a new row referencing the old one.
+
+## Machine form
+
+`compatibility-matrix.template.json` mirrors this table for doctor/report tooling.
