@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# ext test skeletons
+
+These are the acceptance skeletons named by the L2 spec, not substitute product
+tests. Every behavioural test is `it.skip` until its patch (and for the profile /
+distribution directories, the ext bundle) exists; each skipped test names its
+dependency in a comment directly above it. The unskipped test in each file only
+pins the required contract names or matrix enumeration so a rename cannot quietly
+shrink the acceptance surface.
+
+Run them independently of the upstream package matrix:
+
+```sh
+node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config ext/vitest.config.ts
+```
+
+If the session `TMPDIR` points at a read-only mount, point it at a writable
+directory for the run, e.g. `TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)`; otherwise Vitest cannot create
+its SSR temp directory.
+
+| directory | file | contents | dependency |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| contracts | `0001-history-source.contract.test.ts` | 6 names: default-provider-unchanged, provider-conflict, snapshot-tail-no-gap, two-views-independent, replace-releases-nodes, release-keeps-execution | `patches/0.2.1-rc.3/0001-history-source.patch` |
+| contracts | `0002-mounted-chat.contract.test.ts` | 4 names: mounted-owner-singleton, older-resolves-after-layout, latest-fetches-head, unmount-invalidates-handle | `patches/0.2.1-rc.3/0002-mounted-chat.patch` |
+| contracts | `0003-window-commit.contract.test.ts` | 5 names: measure-before-publish, no-intermediate-paint, cancel-before-commit, cancel-after-commit, stale-token-rejected | `patches/0.2.1-rc.3/0003-window-commit.patch` |
+| profile | `0001-0003-feature-switch-matrix.test.ts` | eight combinations (000…111) + pure profile (no hapi-dsh, no provider) | patches 0001–0003 + ext bundle installer |
+| distribution | `install-idempotency.test.ts` | clean install once, repeat twice with no diff, new manifest stages an immutable release | ext single-tgz bundle |
+| distribution | `override-conflict.test.ts` | user overrides preserved; missing ext package / bad checksum / original-mixed-load fail before activation | ext single-tgz bundle |
+| distribution | `rollback.test.ts` | e1→e2→e1 ×3, staging/switch/health-check injections, 30 s health rollback, ≥2 retained releases | ext single-tgz bundle + upgrade state machine + doctor |
+
+The behavioural bodies must be written against the patched packages under
+`packages/` and the installed profiles, not against this skeleton. The gate
+harness (`ext/scripts/accept-ext.mjs`) is separate: it judges measured datasets
+and does not run these vitest files.
