+# Upstream PR draft: optional history source providers for the Session client
+
+## Summary
+
+Add a provider seam for Session history. A feature extension can register a
+versioned provider that owns the history source of a Session generation before
+that generation is retained. The official Session keeps its execution
+identity, queueing, approvals, reconnection, and persistence semantics; only
+the read side of history comes from the provider, and each reading view (Pane)
+opens its own bounded window on the generation's connection.
+
+With no provider registered, the current behavior is unchanged: the original
+`SessionEventStream` opens and pages exactly as today, no window is created, and
+no conversation scope is exposed.
+
+## Changes
+
+New contract `packages/api/session-controller/src/client/contract/history-source.ts`:
+
+- `HistorySnapshotV1`, `HistoryReadV1`, `HistoryDeltaV1`, `HistoryFeedV1`,
+  `HistorySourceV1`, `HistoryProviderV1`, `HistorySourcesV1`, `Budget`,
+  `HistoryTarget`, `Cursor`, `SourceVersion`;
+- `historyExtension(sessions)` accessor over the new optional
+  `ISessions.historySource` property;
+- `HistorySourceError` with `PROVIDER_CONFLICT`, `STALE_VERSION`,
+  `INVALID_WINDOW`, `CAPACITY_EXCEEDED`, `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE`, `DISPOSED`;
+  cancellation rejects with `AbortError`;
+- frozen `capabilities: { historySource: 1 }`, removable at build time with
+  `DSH_CLIENT_HISTORY_SOURCE=off`.
+
+Session controller wiring:
+
+- `ISession.historyRead?` exposes the generation's `openView(viewId, budget?, signal?)`.
+- `ClientSessions` owns the provider registry and selects the provider in
+  `retain`, before the generation's first open. Several matching providers
+  reject with `PROVIDER_CONFLICT` before any read starts.
+- `SessionHistoryConnection` opens/reuses one feed per view id per generation,
+  and the default Session window follows deltas from the opening snapshot's
+  version. A version gap re-reads the newest window instead of appending across
+  it.
+
+Conversation (`ui-conversation`):
+
+- `ConversationBinding.historyView(viewId)` returns a refcounted reading scope
+  (`ConversationHistoryViewV1`): published `HistoryViewSnapshotV1`, the official
+  assembler read face, `read`, `refresh`, `release`.
+- Window replacement reuses `ConversationNodeAssembler.replaceWindow`; the patch
+  adds no node withdrawal. One page read in flight, one pending navigation;
+  changed-but-unpublished changes are bounded at 256 changes or 1MiB, and
+  overflow resynchronizes from the newest window.
+
+Chat (`ui-chat`):
+
+- `ChatViewInjected.hooks.historyPaging` publishes the attached window's paging
+  facts; the optional `historyPagingConsumer` service supplies them. The older
+  history affordance reads them and falls back to the Session snapshot with no
+  consumer.
+
+## Semantics
+
+- `HistoryFeedV1.changes(after)` must replay every change committed after
+  `after`; consumers subscribe from `initial.version` and never read-then-subscribe.
+- `read(before)` returns the page immediately preceding the cursor, `read(after)`
+  the page immediately following it, `read(latest)` the current head window.
+- Releasing a window releases only its feed; releasing every window leaves the
+  Session generation and its execution running.
+- A provider connection is per Session generation; `resync()` opens a new one for
+  the new generation and releases the previous one.
+
+## Testing
+
+New specs pin the required contract names:
+
+- `packages/api/session-controller/tests/history-source.client.spec.ts`:
+  `default-provider-unchanged`, `provider-conflict`, `snapshot-tail-no-gap`;
+- `packages/client/ui-conversation/tests/history-source.client.spec.ts`:
+  `two-views-independent`, `replace-releases-nodes`, `release-keeps-execution`.
+
+The touched-package suites stay green except the pre-existing unbuilt native
+binding in `projection-discovery.host.spec.ts`. Bundles for the three packages
+build after the host type face is built.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+Additive and opt-in. New members are optional on `ISessions`/`ISession`, so
+existing fakes and consumers compile unchanged. No wire schema, persistence
+format, transport, or execution path changes. The capability is read-only so a
+plugin can select an old-compatible profile instead of probing private state.
+
+## Open questions for upstream review
+
+1. Is one provider per Session generation the right ownership unit, or should the
+   provider registry be scoped per Session (e.g. an address-keyed resolver)?
+2. Should `HistoryReadV1.around` return the target's page rather than a
+   window centred on it, to keep window sizes predictable for very long targets?
+3. The projection-capable `Budget.nodes` field is currently advisory; should the
+   client enforce a derived-node count per window, or leave it to the provider?
