+# Upstream PR draft: mounted Chat control for `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-chat`
+
+## Summary
+
+Expose a versioned control face for one *attached* Chat view. Extensions that
+today have to probe DOM nodes, synthesize wheel gestures, or run a second scroll
+controller beside the official one can instead consume a handle delivered at
+mount and released at unmount, with promises that resolve only after the
+committed window and layout are in place.
+
+The official Chat view keeps sole ownership of the scrollport, reading policy,
+and history paging. With no consumer registered, behavior is unchanged: no
+handle, no reading publication, no extra history work.
+
+## Changes
+
+New module `src/client/contract/mounted-chat.ts`:
+
+- `ReadingSnapshotV1`, `MountedChatV1`, `MountedChatInjectionV1`,
+  `HistoryTarget`, `MountedChatSourceV1`, `MountedChatConsumerV1`;
+- `MountedChatError` with `DISPOSED` / `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE` codes;
+- frozen `capabilities: { mountedChat: 1 }`, removable at build time with
+  `DSH_CLIENT_MOUNTED_CHAT=off`.
+
+New module `src/client/chat/use-mounted-chat.ts`: the controller. Reading facts
+publish from committed layout with a monotonic revision; history operations
+settle from a committed render, so a resolved promise means the content and its
+layout anchoring are applied.
+
+Wiring:
+
+- `contract/slots.ts`: `ChatViewInjected` gains optional `onMountedChat` and
+  `mountedChatSource`.
+- `chat/ChatView.tsx`: delivers one handle per mounted view, `null` on unmount.
+- `chat/use-chat-scroll.ts`: binds live reading/navigation facts and computes the
+  handle only when a consumer asked for it.
+- `chat/use-chat-navigation.ts`: `landKey()` for a durable reveal.
+- `chat/use-chat-viewport.ts`: `scrollToKey()` to align a stable anchor key.
+- `client/apply.ts`: reads the optional `mountedChatConsumer` service and installs
+  the delivery; `client/index.ts` exports the contract and capability.
+
+## Semantics
+
+- `read()` / `subscribe()`: reader anchor, following, `hasOlder`, `busy`.
+- `loadOlder()`: one official older page; resolves after prepend and anchoring.
+- `reveal({ key, seq })`: pages through the official jump loader when the target
+  is outside the window, lands on the node, resolves after commit; unknown keys
+  reject `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE`.
+- `toLatest()`: asks a windowed source for the newest window first
+  (`MountedChatSourceV1.readLatest`); only then lands on the tail. A failed head
+  read rejects and keeps the current window.
+- Unmount disposes the handle: sync calls throw `DISPOSED`, async calls reject.
+  Cancellation rejects with `AbortError`.
+
+## Testing
+
+New spec `tests/mounted-chat.client.spec.tsx` covers the required contract names:
+`mounted-owner-singleton`, `older-resolves-after-layout`, `latest-fetches-head`,
+`unmount-invalidates-handle`, plus `capability-declaration` and failed-head
+preservation. The full `packages/client/ui-chat` suite (52 files, 850 tests) is
+green. `pnpm --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-chat bundle` completes after the
+package type faces are built, and the bundle carries the contract.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+Additive only. No official component props, stores, slot declarations, Session
+calls, or scroll policy change when no consumer is installed. The capability is
+declared read-only so consumers can select an old-compatible profile instead of
+probing private state or comparing package versions.
+
+## Open questions for upstream review
+
+1. Should the consumer service live beside `chatFileMentions` as a context
+   property, or should the injection be a declared slot child?
+2. Should the head-read seam be part of this contract, or move to the
+   window-commit transaction once that lands?
