@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+# Upstream PR draft: transactional window commits for Session history
+
+## Summary
+
+Add a versioned window-commit coordinator to the Session Controller client and
+use it for the official Conversation Pane window and the official Chat reader.
+A window replacement becomes one prepared candidate plus one synchronous
+measure/publish/correct section: the reader is measured immediately before the
+publish, the official assembler performs the layout commit, and the measured
+reader corrects itself in the same task before paint. Cancellation before that
+checkpoint leaves the old window published; cancellation after it completes the
+commit and reports success.
+
+The owner keeps the published window until the commit, so no intermediate window
+is observable, and the token that names a transaction is created by the official
+coordinator, bound to its window, and consumed once.
+
+## Changes
+
+New contract `packages/api/session-controller/src/client/contract/window-commit.ts`:
+
+- `PreparedWindowV1`, `WindowCommitV1` (`prepare` / `commitWindow` / `discard`),
+  `WindowCommitResultV1` / `WindowCommitCorrectionV1`;
+- `WindowReaderMeasurementV1`, `WindowLayoutV1`, `WindowReaderParticipantV1`,
+  `WindowReaderParticipationV1`;
+- `WindowCandidateV1`, `WindowCommitHostV1`, `WindowCommitCoordinatorV1`,
+  `WindowCommitFactoryV1`;
+- `WindowCommitError` using the shared V1 failure codes
+  (`STALE_VERSION`, `INVALID_WINDOW`, `CAPACITY_EXCEEDED`,
+  `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE`, `DISPOSED`); cancellation is an `AbortError`;
+- frozen `capabilities: { windowCommit: 1 }`, removable at build time with
+  `DSH_CLIENT_WINDOW_COMMIT=off`.
+
+New implementation `packages/api/session-controller/src/client/sessions/window-commit.ts`:
+the coordinator owns the token table, snapshot validation, capacity checks, the
+candidate lifecycle, and the synchronous critical section.
+
+Wiring:
+
+- `contract/sessions.ts`, `sessions/service.ts`: optional
+  `ISessions.windowCommit` factory, absent when the capability is off.
+- `client/index.ts`: exports the contract, processor factory, capability, error,
+  and default envelope.
+- `ui-conversation/contract conversation assembly`: `ConversationBinding` gains
+  optional `windowCommit: ConversationWindowCommitV1` with
+  `register(viewId, participant)`.
+- `ui-conversation/conversation/assembly.ts`: one coordinator per Pane window;
+  the host builds candidates on a private official assembler and publishes
+  through the live assembler's `replaceWindow` + `flush`.
+- `ui-conversation/conversation/history-view.ts`: opening, `latest`/`around`
+  page reads, live replace deltas, and resync go through
+  `prepare` + `commitWindow`; incremental prepend/append keep the official path.
+- `ui-conversation/conversation/assembler.ts`: read-only
+  `derivedNodeCount()` for capacity evidence.
+- `ui-chat/contract/slots.ts`: optional `ChatViewInjected.windowCommit`
+  participation face.
+- `ui-chat/chat/use-chat-scroll.ts`: registers one measurement/correction
+  participant built from the official viewport; it never takes scroll ownership.
+- `ui-chat/chat/ChatView.tsx`, `client/apply.ts`, `client/index.ts`:
+  thread the participation face from the Conversation binding to the reader.
+
+No second renderer, no incremental node withdrawal, no new scroll controller.
+
+## Semantics
+
+- `prepare(snapshot, signal)`: validates the snapshot (source version, entry
+  list, cursors, range flags, ascending sequence) and its event/byte envelope;
+  builds the candidate derived state and enforces the node envelope. A failing
+  candidate build reports `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE`; every failure keeps the published
+  window. Cancellation before or during prepare rejects with `AbortError`.
+- `commitWindow(prepared, signal)`: consumes the token, checks cancellation and
+  that the window revision still equals `baseRevision`, then runs one
+  synchronous section: measure participants → `host.publish` → participant
+  correction. A `publish` failure reports `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE` and discards the
+  candidate. Cancellation after the checkpoint does not roll back.
+- Completion distinguishes the two sides of the publish: a reader measurement
+  failure happens before it and rejects with `TARGET_UNAVAILABLE` (old window
+  stays), while a reader correction failure happens after it and resolves
+  `{ committed: true, revision, correction: 'failed', correctionError }`. A
+  failed correction is never reported as a clean success; the caller can decide
+  whether to retry it.
+- `discard(prepared)`: drops the candidate; unknown or spent tokens are ignored,
+  and a later commit of the same token reports `STALE_VERSION`.
+- Tokens: coordinator-created, window-bound, single-use. Caller-constructed
+  tokens report `INVALID_WINDOW`; copies of a valid prepared object fail the
+  identity check.
+
+## Default-path invariance
+
+Without the capability or without a Session history provider, the sessions
+factory is absent, no coordinator or participant exists, and the Conversation
+binding publishes through its original `replaceWindow` path. Existing call sites
+do not change shape; all additions are optional properties.
+
+## Testing
+
+- `packages/api/session-controller/tests/window-commit.client.spec.ts` covers
+  `measure-before-publish`, `no-intermediate-paint`, `cancel-before-commit`,
+  `cancel-after-commit`, `stale-token-rejected`,
+  `correction-failure-is-not-success` (the real coordinator reports the published
+  revision and the failed correction as separate facts), plus stale revision,
+  invalid snapshot, capacity, candidate/publish failure, measurement failure,
+  disposal, and no-network-in-critical-section.
+- `packages/client/ui-conversation/tests/history-source.client.spec.ts` adds
+  Conversation-side `measure-before-publish`, `no-intermediate-paint`,
+  `correction-failure-is-not-success` (the Pane window snapshot carries
+  `correction: 'failed'` beside the committed replacement),
+  `registers-reader-before-window`, and `extension-absent-keeps-original-publish`.
+- `packages/client/ui-chat/tests/window-commit.client.spec.ts` covers the reader
+  participant measurement/correction, `correction-failure-is-not-success` (the
+  reader propagates its correction rejection instead of swallowing it), and
+  registration disposal.
+- Build: `tsc -b tsconfig.client.json tsconfig.host.json` (pre-existing generated
+  remote declaration errors recorded, none in the touched files) and tsdown
+  bundle for the three packages.
+
+## Not in this change
+
+- Live streaming deltas are not window commits; they keep their publication
+  path.
+- Pane-window rendering itself is 0001's optional reading scope; this patch
+  only owns how a replacement of that window commits.
