+# Upstream PR draft: keep process groups in the transcript scroll flow
+
+## Problem
+
+The process-group body is a second vertical scrollport. On touch devices, upward movement over a tool group is consumed there, so the history reader never sees a continuous gesture and cannot reliably prefetch older pages.
+
+## Change
+
+Use the process-group title as a disclosure: closed groups show a bounded preview, while opening a group expands all members into the transcript's normal flow. Remove the per-group scroll-follow controller and internal scroll markers. The Conversation viewport remains the only scroll owner.
+
+## Validation
+
+The client component test checks the preview-to-expanded transition. HAPI DSH's real-browser release smoke checks that no process-group body is a scrollport, then validates real desktop wheel and mobile touch paging, committed-page anchors, return-to-bookmark behavior, and frame gaps.
+
+This is a draft for upstream review and has not been submitted.
